{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Affeḥ he cherished the peoples.</b> As it is written, 'You shall be to Me a treasure.' And why? For <b>all his holy ones are in your hand.</b> How so? <b>And they sat at your feet</b> — the meaning is within your feet, as it is written, 'And they stood at the bottom of the mountain.' Another interpretation: even when HaShem cherishes the nations and delivers Israel into their hands — <b>all his holy ones</b> of Israel <b>are in your hand, and they</b> — Israel — <b>are stricken at your feet</b> — for your sake and for your commandments they are struck and crushed." "<b>At your feet.</b> Like 'and may YHWH bless you לרגלי.' Another interpretation: <b>and they are stationed at your feet</b> — within the Temple, which is the footstool of your feet; there they are found." "<b>They bore the utterance of.</b> They took up and bore with a cheerful countenance the two things that issued from your mouth: 'I am' and 'You shall not have.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:20.440829834Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}